# /etc/nsswitch.conf snippet — Nostr + winbind co-existence
#
# Plan §4.3 C2 (Finding 15).  DO NOT install this as
# /etc/nsswitch.conf directly; splice the `passwd:` / `group:` /
# `shadow:` lines into the distribution-installed nsswitch.conf.  The
# ordering matters and is the ENTIRE point of this snippet — the C
# side of nss_nostr does not admit qualified names like `DOMAIN\user`
# or `user@REALM`, so the safety property comes from making sure
# winbind sees those names first.
#
# Required ordering:
#
#     passwd: files winbind nostr
#     group:  files winbind nostr
#     shadow: files
#
# Why `winbind` comes BEFORE `nostr`:
#
#   1. The Nostr NSS module (libnss_nostr.so.2) admits ONLY names
#      matching `^n_[a-z0-9_]+$` — this is enforced in
#      gnome/nostr-homed/src/identity/identity_common.c:8-20 and MUST
#      NOT change.  Domain-qualified names never pass that gate.
#
#   2. If `nostr` were listed BEFORE `winbind`, a lookup for e.g.
#      `EXAMPLE\alice` would still be routed to nss_nostr first,
#      returning NOTFOUND correctly — but the correct answer for that
#      lookup is winbind's positive answer.  With `nostr` after
#      `winbind`, `EXAMPLE\alice` hits winbind first (positive) and
#      never reaches nostr.
#
#   3. `files` stays first so root and other local system accounts
#      never depend on any network module.  This is the distribution
#      default and MUST NOT be dropped.
#
#   4. `shadow` intentionally stays as `files` only — neither nostr
#      nor winbind own the shadow database; Nostr accounts do not
#      have local password hashes and winbind delegates auth via PAM.
#
# When to install this snippet:
#
#   - Standalone Nostr host, no winbind:      OMIT `winbind` from the
#                                             lines above.
#   - Nostr host that has ALSO joined a
#     realm via `net ads join`:               Install the snippet as
#                                             shown; winbind will
#                                             answer for domain names,
#                                             nostr for n_ names.
#   - Neither: do not install nostr in
#     nsswitch at all.
#
# Packaging:
#
#   The distribution package MUST NOT overwrite /etc/nsswitch.conf.
#   Ship this file as `nsswitch.conf.snippet` under the package's
#   documentation directory; a post-install helper OR the administrator
#   splices the lines above.  See gnome/nostr-homed/docs/SAMBA_AD_LOGIN.md
#   for the manual-join recipe that references this ordering.

passwd: files winbind nostr
group:  files winbind nostr
shadow: files
